SUMMARY:Disposable Humanity – FREE
DESCRIPTION:Tuesday\, November 17\, 2026 • 7 PM • Steinman Hall In Disp
 osable Humanity\, the Mitchell family—esteemed Disability Studies schola
 rs and filmmakers—delve into the chilling legacy of the Nazi Aktion T4 p
 rogram. This investigative documentary recounts the long-obscured history 
 of how over 300\,000 disabled individuals became the initial victims of th
 e Third Reich. Targeted by the T4 program as having a “life unworthy of 
 living\,” their murders laid the groundwork for the Holocaust that follo
 wed. 6:15 PM • Pre-show community panel discussion Post-show • Q&A wit
 h director Cameron Mitchell Accessibility: The film is captioned\, and liv
 e captioning (CART) and ASL interpreting will be provided for the panel di
 scussion. Please get in touch with Barry Kornhauser to learn more. Co-pres
 ented by the MU Disability Film Festival and Congregation Shaarai Shomayim
 . Live captioning (CART) supported by the MU Office of Learning Services.\
